  {
    "@id": "https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/SeabedGeomorphologySettings",
    "https://prez.dev/identifier": [
      {
        "@value": "ns1:SeabedGeomorphologySettings"
      }
    ],
    "https://prez.dev/link": [
      {
        "@value": "/catalogs/catalogue:default/collections/ns1:SeabedGeomorphologySettings"
      }
    ],
    "https://prez.dev/label": [
      {
        "@value": "Seabed geomorphology - Part 2 Geomorphology",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "https://prez.dev/description": [
      {
        "@value": "A vocabulary of GEOMORPHIC UNIT terms (Part 2) used in the two-part marine and coastal geomorphology classification scheme (International Seabed Geomorphology Mapping Working Group - ISGM-WG: Part 1 Morphology: [https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.4071940](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.4071940); Part 2 Geomorphology: [https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7804019](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7804019) to classify MORPHOLOGY FEATURES (Part 1) with their process interpretation. These UNIT terms are structured within a consistent framework design that is replicated between eleven SETTING and PROCESS categories.\n\nThis is one of four linked ISGM-WG vocabularies. Definitions in this vocabulary are subject to intermittent review and versioning. Unless otherwise stated, all definitions are derived from the Part 2 Geomorphology report (Version 1.0) [https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7804019](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7804019)).",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "https://prez.dev/members": [
      {
        "@value": "/catalogs/catalogue:default/collections/ns1:SeabedGeomorphologySettings/items"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/SeabedGeomorphologySettings/complex_pockmark",
    "https://prez.dev/identifier": [
      {
        "@value": "ns1:complex_pockmark"
      }
    ],
    "https://prez.dev/link": [
      {
        "@value": "/catalogs/catalogue:default/collections/ns1:SeabedGeomorphologySettings/items/ns1:complex_pockmark"
      }
    ],
    "https://prez.dev/label": [
      {
        "@value": "'complex' pockmark (BGU-T)",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "https://prez.dev/description": [
      {
        "@value": "A cluster of ’NORMAL’ POCKMARKS or amalgamations of larger POCKMARKS.",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/SeabedGeomorphologySettings/giant_pockmark",
    "https://prez.dev/identifier": [
      {
        "@value": "ns1:giant_pockmark"
      }
    ],
    "https://prez.dev/link": [
      {
        "@value": "/catalogs/catalogue:default/collections/ns1:SeabedGeomorphologySettings/items/ns1:giant_pockmark"
      }
    ],
    "https://prez.dev/label": [
      {
        "@value": "giant pockmark (BGU-T)",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "https://prez.dev/description": [
      {
        "@value": "A POCKMARK measuring more than 250 m in diameter. This large-scale seepage structures, that may reach diameters >500 m and up to 1–1.5 km across, have been described as the result of very long period of seepage (e.g. Wenau et al., 2017).",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/SeabedGeomorphologySettings/normal_pockmark",
    "https://prez.dev/identifier": [
      {
        "@value": "ns1:normal_pockmark"
      }
    ],
    "https://prez.dev/link": [
      {
        "@value": "/catalogs/catalogue:default/collections/ns1:SeabedGeomorphologySettings/items/ns1:normal_pockmark"
      }
    ],
    "https://prez.dev/label": [
      {
        "@value": "'normal' pockmark (BGU-T)",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "https://prez.dev/description": [
      {
        "@value": "A POCKMARK, typically measuring from 10 m up to a few hundred meter in diameter, and from 1 m to 25 m deep. Hovland et al. (2010), suggested that these could manifest periodic or intermittent gas bursts (eruptions), with extended intervening periods of slow, diffusive, and cyclic pore-water seepage.",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/SeabedGeomorphologySettings/pockmark",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/SeabedGeomorphologySettings"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/SeabedGeomorphologySettings/Fluid_Flow_Process"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@value": "A concave crater-like Depression formed by gas and/or fluid expulsion, typically one to tens of meters in diameter but can be up to a few hundred meters wide (Hovland et al., 1987). Pockmarks tend to be characteristic V shaped Depressions, with circular, or elliptical geometry. However, they can also present a W-shaped profile or more complex geometries.",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/SeabedGeomorphologySettings"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@value": "pockmark (BGU)",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower": [
      {
        "@id": "https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/SeabedGeomorphologySettings/complex_pockmark"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/SeabedGeomorphologySettings/giant_pockmark"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/SeabedGeomorphologySettings/normal_pockmark"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/SeabedGeomorphologySettings/strings_of_pockmarks"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/SeabedGeomorphologySettings/unit_pockmark"
      }
    ],
    "https://prez.dev/identifier": [
      {
        "@value": "ns1:pockmark"
      }
    ],
    "https://prez.dev/link": [
      {
        "@value": "/catalogs/catalogue:default/collections/ns1:SeabedGeomorphologySettings/items/ns1:pockmark"
      }
    ],
    "https://prez.dev/type": [
      {
        "@id": "https://prez.dev/FocusNode"
      }
    ],
    "https://prez.dev/label": [
      {
        "@value": "pockmark (BGU)",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "https://prez.dev/description": [
      {
        "@value": "A concave crater-like Depression formed by gas and/or fluid expulsion, typically one to tens of meters in diameter but can be up to a few hundred meters wide (Hovland et al., 1987). Pockmarks tend to be characteristic V shaped Depressions, with circular, or elliptical geometry. However, they can also present a W-shaped profile or more complex geometries.",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/SeabedGeomorphologySettings/strings_of_pockmarks",
    "https://prez.dev/identifier": [
      {
        "@value": "ns1:strings_of_pockmarks"
      }
    ],
    "https://prez.dev/link": [
      {
        "@value": "/catalogs/catalogue:default/collections/ns1:SeabedGeomorphologySettings/items/ns1:strings_of_pockmarks"
      }
    ],
    "https://prez.dev/label": [
      {
        "@value": "strings of pockmarks (BGU-T)",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "https://prez.dev/description": [
      {
        "@value": "UNIT POCKMARKS or small NORMAL POCKMARKS arranged in curvilinear chains or strings, that may be kilometres in length. They are suspected to be a result of fluid focusing along near-vertical FAULTS, flexures, or weakness zones in the upper sedimentary layer (Hovland et al., 2002).",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/def/voc/ga/SeabedGeomorphologySettings/unit_pockmark",
    "https://prez.dev/identifier": [
      {
        "@value": "ns1:unit_pockmark"
      }
    ],
    "https://prez.dev/link": [
      {
        "@value": "/catalogs/catalogue:default/collections/ns1:SeabedGeomorphologySettings/items/ns1:unit_pockmark"
      }
    ],
    "https://prez.dev/label": [
      {
        "@value": "unit pockmark (BGU-T)",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "https://prez.dev/description": [
      {
        "@value": "A very small POCKMARK (typically 1–10 m across and up to 0.5 m deep). This type of Pockmark can be found in isolation, in groups, or in association with larger Pockmark (Hovland and Judd, 1988). Hovland et al., (2010) suggested that unit pockmarks likely manifest cyclic pore-water seepage.",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ]
  },
